        "merged_file_metadata": {
          "name": "GEOSFP_A3dyn_loader",
          "description": "Pure-I/O data loader for GEOS-FP (A3DYN collection): 3-hourly time-averaged 3-D dynamics fields (winds, omega, RH, detrainment) on the native 0.3125°×0.25° global longitude/latitude grid, from the GEOS-Chem GEOS_FP 0.25x0.3125 archive.\n\nThis is one loader half of the geosfp loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §4.1/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, following the esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern). It is PURE I/O: it declares its source (url_template), the file variables it reads (with units), its temporal cadence, and its NATIVE grid expressed as a GDD Grid with a geographic (longlat/WGS84) crs descriptor. It performs NO reprojection and NO regridding — those are per-variable concerns of the regridding model (components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm), which references this file as a subsystem via {\"ref\": \"./geosfp_a3dyn_loader.esm\"} under the subsystem key GEOSFP_A3dyn.\n\nThe removed co-located blocks: the old DataLoaderSpatial block (proj4 crs string / grid_type / staggering / resolution / extent) is replaced by the GDD `grid` (family + crs + dimensions + extents); the old per-loader `regridding` block (fill_value / extrapolation) is gone — regridding is declared per-variable on the model (geosfp.esm `regrid`). Because a `temporal` block is present, this loader seeds DISCRETE cadence (ess-v9a.5): the runtime refreshes the file buffers on its update schedule.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, filetype=A3DYN). Split out of the pre-migration components/earthsci_data/geosfp.esm (esm-1c6s).",
